<Article
  title="GTA 6 Heists: Everything Confirmed So Far"
  h1="Heists in GTA 6: What's Confirmed"
  description="What Rockstar has actually confirmed about heists and robberies in GTA 6, from Raul Bautista to the 'easy score goes wrong' story, and what's still speculation."
  published="2026-10-14"
  crumbs={[{ href: "/gta-6/", label: "GTA 6" }]}
  faq={faq}
  sources={[
    { href: "https://www.rockstargames.com/VI", label: "Rockstar Games: Grand Theft Auto VI" },
    { href: "https://www.videogameschronicle.com/news/gta-6s-cast-of-characters-revealed/", label: "VGC: GTA 6's cast of characters revealed" },
  ]}
>
  <p>GTA 6 launches <a href="/gta-6/release-date/">November 19, 2026</a>, and robbery is at the heart of it. But a lot of what you'll read online about GTA 6 heists is guesswork. Here's what Rockstar has actually shown, kept separate from the speculation.</p>

  <h2>Confirmed by Rockstar</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>The story is about a score.</strong> Rockstar's official description says it begins "when an easy score goes wrong" for Lucia and Jason.</li>
    <li><strong>Raul Bautista is a bank robber who recruits crews.</strong> His official character bio calls him a seasoned bank robber who brings in talent for high-risk, high-reward scores.</li>
    <li><strong>Robbery is in the trailers.</strong> The first trailer (December 2023) shows Lucia and Jason holding up a convenience store.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Not confirmed yet</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>A heist planning board or prep missions like GTA 5's</li>
    <li>Choosing a crew, or crew cuts</li>
    <li>Any payout figures</li>
    <li>How many heists there are, or whether you can replay them</li>
    <li>Robbing stores or banks freely in the open world</li>
    <li>What GTA 6's online mode includes</li>
  </ul>
  <div class="callout"><p>Reports of loud vs. quiet approach choices trace back to secondhand coverage of a magazine preview. Rockstar hasn't confirmed them, so treat them as speculation.</p></div>

  <h2>What past GTA games suggest</h2>
  <p>Rockstar's last two big games give a decent template:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>GTA 5 story mode</strong> had five heists with approach and crew choices. The crew you picked changed your take, from a few hundred thousand to over $41 million per character. See <a href="/gta-5-story-mode-heists/">GTA 5 story heist payouts</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>GTA Online</strong> added multi-part heists in 2015 and kept adding them for a decade, from the Fleeca Job to Cayo Perico. See <a href="/gta-online-heist-payouts/">every GTA Online heist payout</a>.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>With a bank-robbing recruiter in the cast, planned heists with crews look likely. How they pay out is anyone's guess until launch.</p>

  <h2>When we'll add GTA 6 heist calculators</h2>
  <p>As soon as we can verify real values in game after November 19. We won't publish guessed numbers. Until then, the <a href="/heist-cut-calculator/">heist cut calculator</a> works for any game: plug in the take and your crew's cuts.</p>
</Article>
